1: # Milestone UI-M1: Scrim, Backdrop & Layout Architecture Report
2: 
3: **Agent**: Explorer 2 (`explorer_ui_m1_2`)  
4: **Mission**: Investigate and design the layout changes in `app/css/layout.css` to introduce Google TV `#shade` dual-gradient crossfading scrim, `#bgBlur` low-cost blurred backdrop, and top pill navigation bar positioning/scrolling behavior.  
5: **Date**: 2026-11-05T01:10:00Z  
6: 
7: ---
8: 
9: ## 1. Executive Summary
10: 
11: This investigation designs the modernized layout architecture for the CineJoy LG webOS application (`com.cinejoy.tv`), transitioning from the legacy deep-forest obsidian background (`#04120B` / radial green gradient `#0a2517`) to the Google TV / cinema-grade design system exemplified by `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/`.
12: 
13: The core architectural components designed in this report are:
14: 1. **Canvas Constraint & Strict 1080p Lock**: Absolute preservation of `1920x1080` canvas, 5% TV-safe padding (`var(--tv-safe-x): 96px`, `var(--tv-safe-y): 54px`), zero desktop scrollbars (`overflow: hidden; scrollbar-width: none;`), and zero horizontal page scroll across all 6 views (`home`, `movies`, `series`, `search`, `details`, `player`).
15: 2. **Dual-Gradient Scrim (`#shade`)**: A GPU-friendly multi-layer gradient scrim combining a 90° horizontal legibility falloff (`rgba(14,16,20,.95) -> rgba(14,16,20,.7) -> rgba(14,16,20,0)`) for left-aligned hero copy with a 0° vertical grounding gradient (`#0e1014 30% -> rgba(14,16,20,.6) 48% -> rgba(14,16,20,0) 70%`) for content shelf blending. Transitions to `.scrolled #shade { background: rgba(14,16,20,.88); }` on vertical scroll.
16: 3. **Low-Cost Blurred Backdrop (`#bgBlur`)**: An extended fixed layer (`top: -60px; left: -60px; width: calc(100% + 120px); height: calc(100% + 120px);`) with `filter: blur(28px) saturate(1.4) brightness(.7);` and smooth opacity crossfading (`opacity: 0 -> 1` in `0.35s`). This avoids expensive per-frame `backdrop-filter` shader recalculations on the webOS TV Mali GPU by pre-filtering a low-resolution thumbnail and animating only GPU-composited opacity.
17: 4. **Top Pill Navigation Bar Auto-Hide & Safe Positioning**: Fixed header container `.app-header` (84px height, 96px horizontal padding) with dual-state dismissal: Google TV scroll auto-hide (`transform: translateY(-20px); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none;` on `.scrolled`) and media player full hide (`transform: translateY(-100%); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none;` on `.header-hidden`).
18: 5. **Zero-Regression Test Compliance**: Empirically verified against all 127 checks in `tests/adversarial-m2-layout.js` (CDP headless Chromium), `app/test-ui.js` regex constraints, and tier 1-3 test harnesses.
19: 
20: ---
21: 
22: ## 2. Current State Analysis (`app/css/layout.css`)
23: 
24: ### 2.1 Existing Layout Structure
25: Inspection of `app/css/layout.css` reveals the following structure:
26: 
27: ```css
28: /* Lines 19-39: Canvas lock */
29: html, body {
30:   width: var(--canvas-width, 1920px);
31:   height: var(--canvas-height, 1080px);
32:   min-width: 1920px;
33:   min-height: 1080px;
34:   max-width: 1920px;
35:   max-height: 1080px;
36:   background-color: var(--color-bg-base);
37:   overflow: hidden;
38:   scrollbar-width: none;
39: }
40: 
41: /* Lines 50-56: Root container with green radial gradient */
42: #app {
43:   position: relative;
44:   width: 1920px;
45:   height: 1080px;
46:   overflow: hidden;
47:   background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, #0a2517 0%, var(--color-bg-base) 70%);
48: }
49: 
50: /* Lines 71-92: Header */
51: .app-header {
52:   position: fixed;
53:   top: 0;
54:   left: 0;
55:   width: 1920px;
56:   height: var(--header-height);
57:   padding-left: var(--tv-safe-x);
58:   padding-right: var(--tv-safe-x);
59:   display: flex;
60:   justify-content: space-between;
61:   align-items: center;
62:   z-index: 100;
63:   background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(4, 18, 11, 0.85) 0%, rgba(4, 18, 11, 0) 100%);
64:   transition: opacity 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease;
65: }
66: 
67: .app-header.header-hidden {
68:   opacity: 0;
69:   transform: translateY(-100%);
70:   pointer-events: none;
71: }
72: ```
73: 
74: ### 2.2 Shortcomings of Existing Implementation
75: 1. **Canvas Tint**: `#app` uses a legacy radial gradient (`radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, #0a2517 0%, var(--color-bg-base) 70%)`) that gives a green halo across the entire TV screen. This conflicts with the Google TV cinema aesthetic (`#0e1014`).
76: 2. **Missing Scrim Architecture**: The existing code has no `#shade` dual-gradient overlay or dynamic crossfading backdrop layer. The hero banner relies solely on an internal container gradient (`.hero-gradient-overlay`), which does not blend across full-screen view transitions or backdrop swaps.
77: 3. **No Blurred Backdrop Layer**: Lacks `#bgBlur`. When content is scrolled up, shelf cards overlap raw backdrop art without a soft frosted/blurred background.
78: 4. **Header Scroll Dynamics**: `.app-header` only has `.header-hidden` (triggered explicitly when entering the video player). It does not implement the Google TV floating auto-hide behavior (`transform: translateY(-20px); opacity: 0;`) when browsing shelf content down the page.
79: 
80: ---
81: 
82: ## 3. Reference Architecture Analysis (`theboringtv-lgwebos`)
83: 
84: ### 3.1 Dual-Gradient Scrim (`#shade`)
85: In `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/style.css` (lines 8-15):
86: ```css
87: #bg, #shade { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
88: #shade {
89:   background:
90:     linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(14,16,20,.95) 0%, rgba(14,16,20,.7) 32%, rgba(14,16,20,0) 62%),
91:     linear-gradient(0deg, #0e1014 30%, rgba(14,16,20,.6) 48%, rgba(14,16,20,0) 70%);
92:   transition: background .4s;
93: }
94: .scrolled #shade { background: rgba(14,16,20,.88); }
95: ```
96: 
97: #### Dual-Gradient Mechanics:
98: - **Horizontal Legibility Gradient (`90deg`)**:
